{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>May YHWH bless you and keep you.</b> In explaining the formula of the blessings, opinions abound; each person according to his intellect interprets them. And in the Yalkut (§605) you will find many opinions — let them be sought from their place, and there is no need to elaborate on their mention. But I say, as a general principle: since all the blessings begin with a yod, from which what is hidden amounts to the number ten just like what is revealed — for what is hidden from the yod is vav and dalet, giving ten — understand from this that all the blessings are doubled, for part of them pertains to the body and part of them pertains to the soul that is concealed, for both of them come to the number ten. As the Sages said (Niddah 31a): there are three partners in a person. The father contributes the white in him, from which come sinews, bones, the brain in his head, fingernails, and the white of the eyes — that is five. The mother contributes the red in him, from which come skin, flesh, blood, hair, and the black of the eyes — that is five. And the Holy One, blessed be He, places in him ten spiritual things, and they are: spirit (ru'ah), soul (neshamah), the countenance of the face, sight of the eye, hearing of the ear, speech of the mouth, walking of the legs, knowledge (da'at), understanding (binah), and intelligence (haskel). And all these twenty parts are blessed through the priest's raising his ten fingers, so that from each finger the blessing may flow upon a physical, revealed part and upon a spiritual, hidden part. And the three yods, that is sixty, correspond to the sixty letters that are in all the blessings, concerning which they expounded (Yalkut Shim'oni, Song §984) the verse (Song 3:7), ״שִׁשִּׁים גִּבּוֹרִים סָבִיב לָהּ״ — 'sixty mighty men surround it.' And the three yods, that is thirty, are joined to the standard nezirut of thirty days, to tell you that through the merit of nezitur they merit the blessings." "And by way of allusion one may explain these three blessings according to what I explained above in parashat Yitro (Exodus 19:4), following the Midrash (Shir haShirim Rabbah 3:21), which says that at first the Holy One, blessed be He, called Israel 'daughter,' and afterward 'sister,' and afterward 'mother' — for all of this signifies the degree of dominion. For at first He called her 'daughter,' for presumably the father rules over the daughter, and He is above and the daughter below; therefore it says ״יְבָרֶכְךָ ה׳ וְיִשְׁמְרֶךָ״ — that the flow of blessings be drawn from above, for He is your keeper, and every keeper stands above the one kept, as it is written (Proverbs 6:22) ״בְּשָׁכְבְּךָ תִּשְׁמֹר עָלֶיךָ״, and so are many verses. And afterward He called her 'sister,' likening Himself to her. On this level it is said ״יָאֵר ה׳ פָּנָיו אֵלֶיךָ״ — when you stand opposite Him face to face, in the manner of the moon's receiving its light from the sun when it stands opposite it. And afterward He called her 'mother,' who rules over the daughter; thus the righteous person rules through the fear of YHWH, just as the daughter's eyes are lifted toward the mother, so YHWH will lift His countenance toward you, as it were. And one need not elaborate on these matters, but they are sound to those who seek understanding."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ו׳ ד׳ שעולה למספר עשרה' is translated literally: the hidden letters that complete the full spelling of יו״ד are ו״ד, and the numerical value of י+ו+ד = 10, matching the manifest yod's own value of 10."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:39:59.874538417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}